@startuml test-status-flow
title Test status flow (TestStatus)

hide empty description
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor<<frozen>> #DDEBF7
  BorderColor<<frozen>> #2F5597
  BackgroundColor<<terminal>> #F8D7DA
}

state CREATED : test persisted,\ngeneration running
state GENERATED : no question needs review
state REQUIRES_REVIEW : ≥ 1 question NEEDS_REVIEW
state REVIEWED : every flagged question resolved\nby a review action
state FAILED <<terminal>> : generation threw
state PUBLISHED <<frozen>> : content frozen,\nonly status that accepts attempts

[*] --> CREATED : POST /api/tests\n(persistTest)

CREATED --> GENERATED : generation done,\nno flags
CREATED --> REQUIRES_REVIEW : generation done,\n≥ 1 option flagged
CREATED --> FAILED : exception
FAILED --> [*]

REQUIRES_REVIEW --> REVIEWED : last flagged question resolved\n(accept fix / regenerate / manual replace)
GENERATED --> REQUIRES_REVIEW : regenerated question\ncomes back flagged
REVIEWED --> REQUIRES_REVIEW : regenerated question\ncomes back flagged

GENERATED --> PUBLISHED : POST /publish
REVIEWED --> PUBLISHED : POST /publish

PUBLISHED --> GENERATED : POST /unpublish\n[no attempts, was GENERATED]
PUBLISHED --> REVIEWED : POST /unpublish\n[no attempts, was REVIEWED]

note right of PUBLISHED
  Review actions return 409.
  Publish and every review action lock the
  test row (SELECT … FOR UPDATE) and check
  the status under the lock.
  Unpublish restores previousStatus from the
  latest TEST_PUBLISHED event (fallback REVIEWED).
end note

note bottom of REQUIRES_REVIEW
  Review actions are allowed in
  GENERATED, REQUIRES_REVIEW and REVIEWED.
  Publish is not allowed here (409).
end note

@enduml
